34,2,,status,Minako,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
35,2,,status,Yumi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
36,2,,status,Benjamin,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
37,2,,status,Daisuke,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
38,2,,status,Shion,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
39,2,1,talk,Yumi,,"Oh no! I just found out that some people in the outer wards have to travel an hour now because of the bus rerouting! That's so sad, we have to find a way to help them!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"It is a sobering realization, Yumi. Interestingly, my research suggests that when we actually went to those outer wards in the past, the response was remarkably high—surpassing our own midweek attendance. The demand is clearly there.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,1,talk,Shion,,"Demand is irrelevant if we can't manage it. I've found that while we have skilled volunteers, we have zero staff trained to supervise outside facilitators. We're essentially flying blind if we add complex new services.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,1,talk,Minako,,"The funding structure is problematic. The grant only covers the first year, and we are letting equipment funds lapse back into reserves while running costs are over budget. We cannot afford a plan with high recurring costs.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I also saw the bus situation. It's really bad. And the roads north of the river close often in winter, but the community halls there still stay open. Maybe we shouldn't expect people to come to us.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Yumi,,"@Daisuke, you're exactly right! If the community halls can stay open while the roads are closed, maybe we should bring the library to them instead of making them travel so far! That would be so helpful!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"A most logical conclusion. It seems we are rediscovering a truth our own records already held: the outer wards are eager for our services, provided we are the ones making the journey.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,2,talk,Shion,,"@Benjamin, your ""truth"" ignores the logistics. If we move services to those halls, who supervises them? My findings show our staff lack the training to manage outside facilitators. We can't just wish a plan into existence.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,2,talk,Minako,,"@Shion, the lack of supervision training is a hurdle, but not an impossible one. However, we must address the budget. If we move services, we must ensure the running costs don't spiral like last year's vehicle lines.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I agree with Shion that we need to be careful. But if we don't do something, the people in the outer wards are just... forgotten. Maybe there's a way to do it without spending too much?","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Yumi,,"@Minako, maybe we can use some of those equipment funds to make it work? I just can't stand the thought of people being left out! Let's find a way to be both sustainable and kind!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Yumi, kindness is a noble aim, but sustainability is its only guardian. If we look at the partner-run groups from six years ago, they survived precisely because they were unaided. Perhaps a self-sustaining model is the answer.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,3,talk,Shion,,"@Benjamin, ""unaided"" is just another word for ""unsupervised."" If we ignore the skill gap in our staff, we aren't being sustainable; we're being negligent. We need a plan that fits our actual roster, not a fantasy.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,3,talk,Minako,,"@Benjamin, a self-sustaining model is ideal, but we must be realistic. @Shion, the training gap is a management issue we can solve. The real danger is the funding cliff after year one. We need a proposal with low recurring costs.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Benjamin"",""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I don't want to argue. I just think... if we only look at the budget and the training, we might forget that some people literally can't get here. Please, can we find a way to reach them?","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Yumi,,"@Daisuke, I'm right here with you! We can't forget them. @Minako, @Shion, if we find a proposal that uses the community halls, it solves the travel problem and might keep costs low! Let's look for that!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Daisuke"",""Minako"",""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,"It seems we have reached a rare moment of alignment. If we seek a proposal that leverages existing community spaces and minimizes our direct overhead, we may finally stop repeating the mistakes of our predecessors. I am ready.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,2,4,talk,Shion,,"I'll play along for now. But let's be clear: if the proposal requires staff to manage things they aren't trained for, I'll be the first to point out the flaw. I'm ready to see the candidates.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,2,4,talk,Minako,,I agree. We need a proposal that balances accessibility with a sustainable financial model. I will be looking for a plan that avoids high recurring costs and utilizes existing infrastructure. I am ready.,"{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,2,4,talk,Daisuke,,I... I'm glad we're all agreeing to think about the people who can't reach us. I'll do my best to help pick the one that's most fair. I'm ready too.,"{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,3,,status,Minako,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
